# Diagnose

Follow the debugging methodology in @process/debugging.md - read it in full before touching code.

## Before you start

- If @CONTEXT.md exists, read it for domain terms.
- If @docs/local/CONCERNS.md exists, check for related open concerns.
- If ADRs exist in @docs/adr/, check the ones in the area you are touching.

## Execution rules

### Hypotheses (Phase 3)

Generate 3-5 ranked hypotheses before testing any of them.
Present the ranked list to the user using the ask tool and wait for confirmation before proceeding.
The user often has domain knowledge that re-ranks instantly.

### Instrumentation (Phase 4)

Tag every debug log with `[DEBUG-xxxx]` (random 4-char hex per session).
One variable at a time. Prefer debugger breakpoints over log lines.
Grep for the tag prefix during cleanup.

### Fix (Phase 5)

Write a failing regression test BEFORE the fix.
Watch it fail for the right reason. Then apply the fix. Then watch it pass.
If no correct test seam exists, note that as a finding for architectural improvement.

### Cleanup (Phase 6)

Before declaring done:
- Original repro no longer reproduces
- Regression test passes
- All `[DEBUG-...]` logs removed (grep the prefix)
- Root cause stated in the commit message
